WEBVTT

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:06.020
The newspaper association hasn't 
taken any action since then.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.220
Well, they wouldn't just let 
themselves be grabbed by the tail.

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:13.270
<b>Running Speed by Class 
 Number 1</b>

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:13.380
Please let me go!

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:13.890
<b>Bottom Rung</b>

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:16.490
What is it you guys want?

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:19.230
You called Mizushima-senpai your old enemy.

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:20.910
Do you have some grudge against her?

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:24.850
She's cruel.

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:27.780
When I went to her to protest our low budget...

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:31.920
The paper's working on something 
interesting right now.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.220
We need a single-lens reflex camera

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:37.660
and the newest computer and 
design software we can get.

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:39.930
We need a scanner and a laser printer, too.

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:41.800
Let me tell you one thing.

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:44.400
Don't underestimate money.

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:48.740
We were demoted from a club 
to an association after that,

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:50.590
and we lost our room.

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:52.280
The way she said it aside...

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:53.570
It seems like it couldn't be helped.

00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:57.740
I thought you were allies of the weak!

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:00.310
I'm disappointed in Princess Fuji!

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:01.360
Princess Fuji?

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.900
Yeah, that's your embarrassing nickname.

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:06.420
I'm disappointed in the Wild Kid, too!

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:10.090
You're so mean!

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:16.250
<b>The Wild Kid              The Wild Kid              The Wild Kid</b>

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:16.260
The Wild Kid... the Wild Kid... the Wild Kid...

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:19.120
Was she talking about me?

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:21.970
Riko, hang in there! Riko!

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:58.010
<b>To the Wild Kid...</b>

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:02.280
There's no deep meaning 
behind "the Wild Kid."

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:04.660
Don't take it so seriously.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:07.160
If anything, it's proof of your popularity.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:09.160
So, stop doing that.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:11.780
Goodness.

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:13.380
Whatever are you talking about?

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:16.460
Honestly, it's kind of creepy.

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:19.420
Oh, Senpai, you're so mean.

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:20.780
There.

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:22.490
There, there.

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:24.350
Whap, whap, whappity-whap!

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:27.220
Sh-She's making sound effects...

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:29.740
Get it together!

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:32.150
If you don't snap back at her, who will?

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:34.520
I... really can't...

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:41.030
What beautiful flowers.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:47.200
C-Can I help you?

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:52.620
My family told me you're the kind 
of girl who's truly feminine, Maki.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:55.040
That's why I'm studying you.

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:58.800
Who, me? But...

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:03.680
I won't let anyone call me 
by that nickname any more.

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:06.880
It can't be helped. 
That's how you really are.

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:08.850
Besides, it's not an insult.

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:11.070
I don't care, I don't like it!

00:04:11.070 --> 00:04:13.310
What is "Wild Kid" supposed to mean, anyway?

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:16.560
It sounds like I'm someone 
who gnaws on raw meat!

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:22.900
<i>I didn't think she would hate it so much...</i>

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:22.890
<b>Called her the Wild Kid</b>

00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:26.090
The abbreviation sounds like 
"Waki," which means...

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:27.410
"armpit"...

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:28.390
Gulp!

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:34.780
<b>Called her W-K</b>

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:32.410
Come to think of it, you called me that before...

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:34.790
Suzu-chan, is that how you see me?

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:38.340
N-No! I think your armpits are wonderful!

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:41.760
I only hope to have armpits like yours someday!

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:44.680
That's not what I meant!

00:04:45.530 --> 00:04:49.140
C-Come on, let's stop talking about this.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:53.810
R-Riko, let's talk about the 
newspaper association, okay?

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:55.640
Let's do that, okay?

00:04:56.030 --> 00:04:58.580
Actually, perhaps we shouldn't today.

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:01.290
What? Why not?

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:04.740
According to Ichikawa-san,

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:08.130
she seems upset she was 
demoted from a club.

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:09.510
You're right.

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:13.410
It's because you're too harsh.

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:14.380
Bad!

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:17.330
You're being more than just a little annoying.

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:20.630
I made the final decision to demote them.

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:22.960
They should hate me, too.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:26.150
It must have happened while no one 
knew you were the president.

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:30.300
You really are more than 
just a little annoying.

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:35.270
The newspaper association currently seems 
to be borrowing the broadcasting room.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:37.820
I wonder why they decided to act now.

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:41.980
If there's a reason, perhaps it was because of...

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:44.360
That! Broad! Cast!

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:46.080
Are you messing with me?!

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:47.200
That's what I should be asking!

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:48.570
That's what <i>I</i> should be asking!

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:51.250
Excuse me.

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:53.040
I'm from the broadcasting club.

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:54.760
Can we help you?

00:05:56.020 --> 00:06:01.340
We put a request box outside the 
broadcasting room last week,

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:04.250
and we found this inside.

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:09.680
"I'd like to hear Princess Fuji 
and the Wild Kid sing a duet."

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:12.890
Oh, I'm sorry. I meant to show you this one.

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:15.970
"After listening to the 
broadcast the other day,

00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:19.900
I have something I'd like 
to ask the student council.

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:23.000
Do boys not like tan girls?"

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:26.070
"What if I'm a little chubby?"

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:30.910
Who suggested you put 
the request box there?

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:34.350
I was talking to Minami-san 
from the newspaper association...

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:37.830
We'll hold onto this for now.

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:40.580
But, due to issues related to the content,

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:42.330
make sure you don't tell 
anyone else about this.

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:43.310
I won't.

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:44.980
Excuse me.

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:51.040
Having another way for people to 
contact us besides our suggestion boxes

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:52.220
is a bit of a problem.

00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:55.390
They're waiting to see what we'll do.

00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:59.290
If we respond to the previous 
requests and ignore this one,

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:00.980
they can say we're playing favorites.

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:03.150
But if we don't respond,

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:06.070
they'll send more requests and 
create even more pressure.

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:09.500
Come on out of Senpai, brilliant solution!

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:12.100
Whap, whap, whappity-whap!

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:13.220
Stop that.

00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:14.460
Nothing's coming out?

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:16.080
Well, that's no good.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:19.330
Oh, I know. I'll ask the flowers.

00:07:19.610 --> 00:07:22.450
Flowers, flowers, do you have any good...

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:23.310
Riko.

00:07:27.690 --> 00:07:29.410
You're so cute.

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:31.360
You're my ideal girl.

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:35.470
Sweet Riko, will you be my princess?

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:37.510
Hey, you've been imitating Maki, right?

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:40.310
Come on, do it.

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:41.600
Do it.

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:44.730
I can't imitate Makio!

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:48.850
<b>The Next Day</b>

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:08.210
You're so mean, soul sister.

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:12.880
Resound, gospel of my soul.

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:16.040
Damn it. I can't believe you can sing well, too.

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:18.310
So, what are you doing?

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:22.700
I was thinking of how to answer the 
question "Do boys like tan girls?"

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:25.400
I was conducting my investigation as a soul singer.

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:29.490
My brother said soul singers have fantastic hips.

00:08:29.490 --> 00:08:32.700
My brother said he wishes they would 
step on him with their long legs.

00:08:32.910 --> 00:08:35.030
Your brothers are really on top of their game...

00:08:35.230 --> 00:08:38.400
What about the question regarding chubby girls?

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:41.000
<i>Didn't Suzu have some kind of...</i>

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:42.850
<i>Weight-related trauma?</i>

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:45.510
It's nothing to worry about.

00:08:45.510 --> 00:08:49.000
They say boys prefer girls 
who are a little chubby.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:51.670
It's better to have breasts 
than to be too skinny.

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:56.110
Hey, say something to her.

00:08:56.110 --> 00:08:57.780
Huh? Like what?

00:08:58.150 --> 00:08:59.240
Oh, I know!

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:01.810
My brother said girls who are 
embarrassed over their small breasts

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:05.350
are totally sweet, totally cute, and totally killer!

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:07.560
Really?

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:10.020
<i>That's the first time Eno's brother 
was good for something!</i>

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:11.420
H-He said all that?

00:09:11.420 --> 00:09:12.820
So even I'm...

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:15.030
But you have breasts.

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:16.530
Suzu turned to the dark side!

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:19.950
I-I guess I was wrong...

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:22.830
Why don't you substitute something 
else you're self-conscious about?

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:25.670
I'm embarrassed I frequently get 
hangnails on my pinkie finger!

00:09:25.670 --> 00:09:29.040
I'm embarrassed to have friends like these!

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:30.960
It's finished.

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:33.680
Let's bring this to the student 
council room immediately.

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:37.660
They'll buckle under this harassment and 
restore our status as a club in no time.

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:39.800
There's no need to rush.

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:42.770
But if we don't, we won't make it in time.

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:47.120
I'd hate it if your article went unappreciated.

00:09:47.370 --> 00:09:48.900
Nana-chan...

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:50.990
I'm going now.

00:09:53.210 --> 00:09:54.640
Ouch...

00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:56.100
Sorry.

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:02.440
<i>It's going to take her a while to get there.</i>

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:07.360
After listening to the 
broadcast the other day,
 I have something I'd like
 to ask the student council.

00:10:03.550 --> 00:10:07.370
They've revealed too much 
about themselves, haven't they?

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:09.490
If they wanted to crush us,

00:10:09.490 --> 00:10:12.790
they could have told the teachers 
about our romantic advice.

00:10:13.070 --> 00:10:16.010
If they wanted a scoop, they 
should have done it secretly.

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:18.580
They told us about their investigation,

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:20.970
went through the trouble 
of making a request box,

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:24.680
and made it obvious they were behind it, 
as though they wanted us to know.

00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:27.550
Perhaps they want to make a trade.

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:31.770
For the promotion of their club 
or an increase in the budget?

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:34.320
Surely you don't mean to accept those terms!

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:35.510
Of course not.

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:36.880
I have everyone's approval

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:39.700
because I use the power of the 
student council appropriately.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:42.160
Appropriately?

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:47.740
Really?

00:10:47.990 --> 00:10:50.460
Excluding times I'm forced to bend the rules.

00:10:51.240 --> 00:10:55.420
I'm curious if they're acting now 
because of that broadcast.

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:58.510
Could there be a reason 
they have to act now?

00:10:58.820 --> 00:11:02.670
My homeroom teacher Sugihara-sensei 
used to be the newspaper club's advisor.

00:11:02.670 --> 00:11:03.970
I'll ask her about it.

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:09.390
I'll examine the materials the student 
council has on the newspaper club.

00:11:09.740 --> 00:11:13.660
Riko, let's split up and question the students.

00:11:13.660 --> 00:11:14.340
Got it.

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:15.720
I'll help.

00:11:15.880 --> 00:11:17.030
Please do.

00:11:17.470 --> 00:11:19.900
Let's prepare ourselves for a counterattack.

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:23.180
Did you get any information?

00:11:23.180 --> 00:11:23.950
No.

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:24.990
Neither did I.

00:11:25.610 --> 00:11:28.360
According to Minami-senpai's classmates,

00:11:28.360 --> 00:11:32.840
some members quit when the newspaper 
club was demoted to an association.

00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:35.130
Maybe the members who 
quit will tell us something.

00:11:35.350 --> 00:11:37.090
Where are they now?

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:39.280
They transferred to other clubs.

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:41.130
Let's split up and go—

00:11:41.910 --> 00:11:43.140
What a surprise.

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:44.310
Why are you here?!

00:11:44.310 --> 00:11:46.220
I saw you on my way to the restroom.

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:49.170
This isn't like you, Sayo-chan.

00:11:49.340 --> 00:11:51.640
You're having so much fun with your friends.

00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:53.810
This isn't where you belong.

00:11:53.810 --> 00:11:55.700
Hey, say something to her.

00:11:55.700 --> 00:11:56.900
It's fine.

00:11:57.250 --> 00:11:58.480
How?

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:00.320
I'm just letting her have her fun.

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:01.860
Just kidding.

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:04.200
Didn't that sound like a 
stereotypical line out of a novel?

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:05.090
Huh?

00:12:05.090 --> 00:12:05.860
What?

00:12:05.860 --> 00:12:06.930
You're such good friends.

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:08.480
That's great, Sayo-chan.

00:12:08.480 --> 00:12:11.660
Oh, by the way, I'm sure you haven't 
gotten one of these yet, so here.

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:12.910
Bye.

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:20.380
What?

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:24.880
That's a pretty nice photo.

00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:25.540
What?

00:12:25.540 --> 00:12:27.870
Maybe the subject was good.

00:12:27.870 --> 00:12:29.100
I should try it again...

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:31.270
It wasn't good at all!

00:12:31.270 --> 00:12:35.540
The photo doesn't convey any of 
the discomfort, but read the article!

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:37.910
"Gone mad"? I couldn't agree more!

00:12:37.910 --> 00:12:39.230
That's going too far.

00:12:39.620 --> 00:12:42.600
Do they mean to distribute 
this throughout the school?

00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:45.990
They'd never get permission 
to distribute this content.

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:48.530
This is kind of interesting.

00:12:48.530 --> 00:12:51.020
"She cannot be called the Wild Kid any longer."

00:12:51.020 --> 00:12:52.880
Oh, I like this!

00:12:52.880 --> 00:12:54.410
"She's the Mild Kid."

00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:57.120
That's not any different...

00:12:57.420 --> 00:12:59.370
I-It's all right.

00:12:59.370 --> 00:13:02.880
If you shorten "Mild Kid," we'll both be Maki!

00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:13.090
<b>President's Aide Gone Mad?!</b>

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:14.100
What?

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:17.540
She's so slow.

00:13:18.240 --> 00:13:20.440
Wait!

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:22.610
I can't!

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:24.570
<i>My chance!</i>

00:13:25.770 --> 00:13:27.300
Now!

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:29.570
I'll get her this time!

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:32.930
<i>Could this be some kind of new game?</i>

00:13:31.340 --> 00:13:32.930
Stay back!

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:34.390
Wait!

00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:39.940
What do you want?

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:41.360
What do I want?

00:13:41.360 --> 00:13:44.100
What is the meaning of this?

00:13:46.070 --> 00:13:47.630
What a nice photo...

00:13:49.400 --> 00:13:55.190
Riko-senpai's unnatural behavior looks 
so natural and cute in this photo.

00:13:55.550 --> 00:13:57.180
R-Really?

00:13:57.180 --> 00:14:00.570
I'm sure Riko-senpai will like this photo.

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:02.070
Y-You think so?

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:03.250
Yes!

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:07.320
What are you doing?

00:14:07.590 --> 00:14:11.740
Senpai, look at what they made!

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:15.660
Senpai!

00:14:15.860 --> 00:14:17.370
The newspaper club?

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:21.530
Yes. It seems they're not 
happy about their demotion.

00:14:21.530 --> 00:14:23.340
Have you heard anything about that?

00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:27.380
I-I'm curious as a member 
of the student council.

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:29.110
I want a seaweed lunch.

00:14:29.110 --> 00:14:30.720
I'm trying to have a serious discussion!

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:35.970
With no new members this year, 
Minami was prepared for the demotion.

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:40.190
It was no surprise their club room
 was converted into storage.

00:14:40.530 --> 00:14:42.060
They lost some members,

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:45.360
but aside from those two, none of 
them really did any work anyway.

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:48.780
Ichikawa said she didn't care as long 
as she could get revenge for last year.

00:14:49.020 --> 00:14:50.160
Revenge?

00:14:50.920 --> 00:14:55.040
They didn't place in last year's 
newspaper contest, did they?

00:14:55.320 --> 00:14:57.360
They didn't? You seem to know a lot.

00:14:57.360 --> 00:14:59.250
Why doesn't their advisor know?

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:02.400
They're not unhappy.

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:06.610
Oh, right. I heard the rules 
for entry changed this year.

00:15:06.750 --> 00:15:10.200
Here. "Associations can no longer participate."

00:15:10.440 --> 00:15:11.010
See?

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:13.130
They <i>are</i> unhappy!

00:15:14.360 --> 00:15:17.520
I brought some important information, but...

00:15:18.940 --> 00:15:20.300
Please forgive me!

00:15:20.300 --> 00:15:21.940
What are you doing?

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:24.520
There's a newspaper contest next month!

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:26.680
This must be why they're acting now!

00:15:26.680 --> 00:15:28.320
They're after a promotion!

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:32.050
I won't say it anymore!

00:15:30.350 --> 00:15:32.050
Listen to me!

00:15:33.220 --> 00:15:35.200
I'm not having a good week.

00:15:35.590 --> 00:15:36.880
And after this...

00:15:36.880 --> 00:15:38.160
Is something happening?

00:15:38.880 --> 00:15:41.040
I'm meeting my boyfriend after school.

00:15:41.880 --> 00:15:44.790
Seriously? You're finally acting like a couple!

00:15:45.410 --> 00:15:48.900
When I ignored our six month 
anniversary and his birthday,

00:15:48.900 --> 00:15:52.430
he emailed me asking if he could ambush 
me on my way home from school.

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:54.720
He's your boyfriend <i>and</i> your stalker.

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:56.060
Ambush...

00:15:57.490 --> 00:16:00.340
Evil

00:15:57.500 --> 00:15:58.920
<i>I've been waiting to ambush you!</i>

00:15:58.920 --> 00:15:59.880
<i>Come with me!</i>

00:16:00.070 --> 00:16:02.440
<i>I've been waiting to ambush your ambush!</i>

00:16:03.050 --> 00:16:05.590
<i>From now on, I only want to ambush you!</i>

00:16:05.590 --> 00:16:06.570
<i>Please.</i>

00:16:07.920 --> 00:16:10.890
<b>Riko learned slapstick 
technique "Fantasy Breaker"!!</b>

00:16:12.250 --> 00:16:14.630
Maybe I'll postpone my date.

00:16:14.760 --> 00:16:16.030
What are you talking about?

00:16:16.030 --> 00:16:17.990
We can handle it ourselves.

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:20.660
You're finally willing to see him, so go.

00:16:21.190 --> 00:16:25.190
Okay, I'll ask him about the request 
we received the other day.

00:16:25.410 --> 00:16:29.180
"What should I say if I just want 
to be friends with my boyfriend?"

00:16:29.180 --> 00:16:30.880
Don't ask him that.

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:33.180
Your first time seeing him in six months!

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:34.550
Where are you meeting him?

00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:35.470
The park.

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:36.750
The park...

00:16:36.750 --> 00:16:37.740
<i>Did you wait long?</i>

00:16:37.740 --> 00:16:39.760
<i>No, I just got here.</i>

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:42.260
Don't fantasize about me!

00:16:42.260 --> 00:16:44.260
Hurry up and break her fantasy!

00:16:44.260 --> 00:16:46.590
What? But it's cute.

00:16:46.590 --> 00:16:48.850
You're not giving him a birthday present?

00:16:48.850 --> 00:16:49.980
No way!

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:51.760
How naïve, Suzu.

00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:56.320
<i>This time with me is...</i>

00:16:56.320 --> 00:16:59.410
<i>my-pre-sent-to-you.</i>

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:02.290
Stop that!

00:17:03.190 --> 00:17:05.620
Am I having a string of bad days?

00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:08.160
See you later.

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:13.560
Now that we've seen off Mizushima-senpai,

00:17:13.560 --> 00:17:16.300
we can focus on how to handle 
the newspaper association.

00:17:18.740 --> 00:17:21.850
The entry deadline for the 
next contest is in ten days.

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:25.850
I believe they'll approach 
us to negotiate soon.

00:17:25.910 --> 00:17:31.760
"Do boys not like tan girls?"
<Student Council's View>
Singer-songwriters are popular.

00:17:25.910 --> 00:17:31.760
"What if I'm a little chubby?"
<Student Council's View>
Rumor has it that's what boys prefer.

00:17:26.470 --> 00:17:28.740
In order to take control of negotiations,

00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:31.780
we'll beat them to the punch by 
delivering these responses beforehand.

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:33.730
You didn't put much thought into those.

00:17:33.730 --> 00:17:35.300
Let me see.

00:17:37.010 --> 00:17:40.740
Did you give me the one about 
chubby girls because I'm chubby?

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:42.620
I-It was just a coincidence.

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:49.820
Newspaper 
Association
 (Temporary)

00:17:44.980 --> 00:17:47.370
My little brother's baseball game is today.

00:17:47.630 --> 00:17:49.830
What about a baseball game?

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:54.700
My parents asked me to take 
pictures, but I have work to do.

00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:57.130
I-I could go for you.

00:17:57.860 --> 00:18:00.360
The secretary complimented my photo.

00:18:00.620 --> 00:18:04.180
I've gotten a little better... I think.

00:18:04.400 --> 00:18:07.350
I'm sure my brother would love your pictures.

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:08.900
Leave it to me!

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:10.450
It's at the local elementary school.

00:18:10.450 --> 00:18:11.270
Got it!

00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:20.520
Sheesh.

00:18:22.440 --> 00:18:23.370
Yes?

00:18:25.380 --> 00:18:26.740
Oh, welcome.

00:18:26.740 --> 00:18:28.840
I brought you what you asked for.

00:18:29.020 --> 00:18:30.820
Did I ask you for something?

00:18:31.090 --> 00:18:33.550
Regarding tan girls and chubby girls.

00:18:33.830 --> 00:18:35.190
What do you think?

00:18:37.490 --> 00:18:41.410
Did you give me the one about chubby 
girls first because I'm chubby?

00:18:41.410 --> 00:18:43.180
I-It was just a coincidence.

00:18:43.930 --> 00:18:45.600
I don't know anything about these.

00:18:45.800 --> 00:18:48.060
Besides, don't you think your 
answers are too halfhearted?

00:18:48.360 --> 00:18:49.850
Do I have the wrong person?

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:51.080
I'm sorry.

00:18:51.080 --> 00:18:54.110
We did our best to answer the questions.

00:18:54.480 --> 00:18:57.360
We had been worried about 
giving romantic advice.

00:18:57.750 --> 00:19:00.030
If we received any more of these requests,

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:02.410
we were considering
 discussing it with the teachers.

00:19:02.680 --> 00:19:04.780
Wouldn't you feel bad for the 
girls who submitted them?

00:19:04.780 --> 00:19:06.300
They're anonymous.

00:19:06.300 --> 00:19:08.780
We have no way of giving them our answers.

00:19:09.770 --> 00:19:12.080
In that case, why don't 
you tell them using this?

00:19:12.940 --> 00:19:15.670
It's an underground paper we 
distribute only to students.

00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:17.840
Tell us more!

00:19:18.200 --> 00:19:19.670
It's basically...

00:19:20.050 --> 00:19:22.620
<i>Oh, no. We need to take control.</i>

00:19:23.150 --> 00:19:25.080
<i>Their weakness is time.</i>

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:27.300
We can't decide right away.

00:19:27.300 --> 00:19:31.230
Let's see... We'll need at 
least ten days to consider.

00:19:33.300 --> 00:19:34.310
Fine.

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:35.480
What?

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:38.550
It's a shame we won't be able to 
participate in the summer contest,

00:19:38.550 --> 00:19:41.320
but it's not that important to me.

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:48.340
She doesn't want revenge for the contest?

00:19:48.530 --> 00:19:49.940
She wasn't offering 
the underground paper

00:19:49.940 --> 00:19:52.560
in exchange for being 
promoted to a club, either.

00:19:52.560 --> 00:19:55.780
The underground paper does seem interesting.

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:58.950
Let's discuss this with everyone tomorrow.

00:19:59.120 --> 00:20:01.480
After Senpai tells us about her date.

00:20:01.480 --> 00:20:03.640
I've got a barrage of questions for her.

00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:07.970
I got some good pictures.

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:10.480
I feel like I really have gotten better.

00:20:10.620 --> 00:20:14.770
It won't be long before I'll scare our 
old enemy Mizushima out of her wits...

00:20:17.630 --> 00:20:18.510
<b>Wits</b>

00:20:17.640 --> 00:20:18.510
<i>Pow!</i>

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:21.850
<b>The Next Day, After School</b>

00:20:23.650 --> 00:20:26.220
<i>I took this without thinking yesterday...</i>

00:20:26.460 --> 00:20:29.120
<i>I had no idea she had a boyfriend.</i>

00:20:29.480 --> 00:20:33.500
<i>Maybe she'll be happy enough the day 
after her date to approve our budget.</i>

00:20:35.410 --> 00:20:36.420
Excuse me.

00:20:37.200 --> 00:20:38.130
What?

00:20:39.170 --> 00:20:40.150
Um...

00:20:40.150 --> 00:20:42.180
Have you been taking candid pictures again?

00:20:42.180 --> 00:20:45.550
Is sneaky photo editing how the 
newspaper association does things?

00:20:48.440 --> 00:20:52.890
Y-You're a member of the student 
council, but you're going on dates!

00:20:53.540 --> 00:20:54.830
Where did you get that picture?

00:20:54.830 --> 00:20:56.430
It's yesterday's scoop!

00:20:56.430 --> 00:20:57.370
Give me that.

00:20:57.370 --> 00:21:00.320
I'm going to submit it to the special 
summer program, "Horror! Dopplegangers."

00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:02.470
You're going to erase it!

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:03.900
Mizushima-san, Ichikawa-san.

00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:07.630
Come to the student guidance office.

00:21:10.070 --> 00:21:11.620
He's just a friend.

00:21:11.990 --> 00:21:17.250
Even if he is, staying out late alone 
with male students is scandalous!

00:21:18.460 --> 00:21:20.040
To think a member of the student council

00:21:20.040 --> 00:21:22.190
is having inappropriate contact with a boy.

00:21:22.510 --> 00:21:25.170
Do Enomoto-san and Maki-san know about this?

00:21:25.580 --> 00:21:27.570
It would be quite the problem if they did.

00:21:36.380 --> 00:21:37.970
It really has been a bad day.

00:21:37.970 --> 00:21:39.900
No, a bad week.

00:21:39.900 --> 00:21:41.320
What are you talking about?

00:21:41.790 --> 00:21:44.990
I had been keeping it a secret 
because I didn't want it to get out.

00:21:45.520 --> 00:21:47.020
If I had known this would happen,

00:21:47.020 --> 00:21:50.870
I would have told everyone else.

00:21:51.560 --> 00:21:53.000
I lied.

00:21:53.220 --> 00:21:54.410
That's my boyfriend.

00:21:54.620 --> 00:21:55.520
What?

00:21:55.520 --> 00:21:57.210
Mizushima-senpai?

00:21:57.800 --> 00:22:01.850
Also, I'll quit the student council.

00:22:03.520 --> 00:22:05.740
I hope Mizushima-senpai will be back soon.

00:22:05.740 --> 00:22:08.220
I want to hear about her date!

00:22:08.520 --> 00:22:11.810
S-S-Suzu, don't be so nervous!

00:22:11.810 --> 00:22:14.680
J-J-Just try to wait calmly!

00:22:12.780 --> 00:22:16.050
Congratulations on Your Six Month 
Anniversary, Mizushima-senpai

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:16.060
<i>You</i> need to calm down.

00:22:16.430 --> 00:22:19.400
It's your own fault if you're let down
because your hopes were too high.

00:22:20.050 --> 00:22:23.200
Anyway, Sayo sure is taking a long time.

00:23:57.470 --> 00:24:03.280
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:57.960 --> 00:24:01.430
<i>Mizushima-senpai can't help with the 
preview because she's on a date.</i>

00:24:01.430 --> 00:24:02.900
<i>I'm so jealous.</i>

00:24:02.900 --> 00:24:04.940
<i>Riko, what kinds of dates 
have you experienced before?</i>

00:24:04.940 --> 00:24:08.840
<i>What? Well, soccer and baseball...</i>

00:24:08.840 --> 00:24:11.300
<i>I see. You go to watch sporting events!</i>

00:24:11.300 --> 00:24:13.070
<i>Yeah, that's it!</i>

00:24:13.070 --> 00:24:15.440
<i>I wonder what kind of date 
Mizushima-senpai is having.</i>

00:24:15.440 --> 00:24:20.480
<i>Last time, she went to banks, stock brokers,
 and real estate firms around town.</i>

00:24:20.480 --> 00:24:22.820
<i>Those are all places that 
deal with lots of money.</i>

00:24:20.950 --> 00:24:27.050
<b>That Smile...</b>

00:24:22.820 --> 00:24:25.280
<i>She never loses focus, does she?</i>

00:24:27.090 --> 00:24:30.100
<b>Don't miss the next episode!</b>
